  - categoryName: WorldController
    entries:
    - key: worldController.introDialog.0
      type: 2
      value: Hold the line! Keep those things off the mothership!
      baseValue: 
      context: 
      aiTranslated: 0
      keptEnglish: 0
    - key: worldController.introDialog.1
      type: 2
      value: More hostiles approaching. They currently outnumber us five to one.
      baseValue: 
      context: 
      aiTranslated: 0
      keptEnglish: 0
    - key: worldController.introDialog.2
      type: 2
      value: This isn't looking good...
      baseValue: 
      context: 
      aiTranslated: 0
      keptEnglish: 0
    - key: worldController.introDialog.4
      type: 2
      value: Anomalous signal detected. It's... a transponder coming from a derelict
        vessel. Its distance is... this range shouldn't be possible.
      baseValue: 
      context: 
      aiTranslated: 0
      keptEnglish: 0
    - key: worldController.introDialog.5
      type: 2
      value: A shipwreck? Are you sure?
      baseValue: 
      context: 
      aiTranslated: 0
      keptEnglish: 0
    - key: worldController.introDialog.6
      type: 2
      value: Positive. Signal strength suggests it's real. But we shouldn't be able
        to detect it at this range.
      baseValue: 
      context: 
      aiTranslated: 0
      keptEnglish: 0
    - key: worldController.introDialog.7
      type: 2
      value: Distance is good! Set course immediately. We'll follow your lead.
      baseValue: 
      context: 
      aiTranslated: 0
      keptEnglish: 0
    - key: worldController.corePanelNavigationDialog.0
      type: 2
      value: We need to work our way through this sector to find the Sector Keystones.
      baseValue: 
      context: 
      aiTranslated: 0
      keptEnglish: 0
    - key: worldController.corePanelNavigationDialog.1
      type: 2
      value: The ship can hyperjump between connected encounters as you explore.
      baseValue: 
      context: 
      aiTranslated: 0
      keptEnglish: 0
    - key: worldController.corePanelUpgradesDialog.0
      type: 2
      value: Welcome to the upgrade system. Try not to break anything.
      baseValue: 
      context: 
      aiTranslated: 0
      keptEnglish: 0
    - key: worldController.corePanelUpgradesDialog.1
      type: 2
      value: Level up to earn upgrade points. Every 10 levels, you get a shiny new
        weapon slot.
      baseValue: 
      context: 
      aiTranslated: 0
      keptEnglish: 0
    - key: worldController.corePanelUpgradesDialog.2
      type: 2
      value: Bigger ships start to unlock at 15... assuming you survive that long.
      baseValue: 
      context: 
      aiTranslated: 0
      keptEnglish: 0
    - key: worldController.corePanelUpgradesDialog.3
      type: 2
      value: No choices are permanent. You can reset it all for free.
      baseValue: 
      context: 
      aiTranslated: 0
      keptEnglish: 0
    - key: worldController.corePanelSlotUnlockedDialog.0
      type: 2
      value: New weapon slot unlocked. Try not to waste it.
      baseValue: 
      context: 
      aiTranslated: 0
      keptEnglish: 0
    - key: worldController.corePanelSlotUnlockedDialog.1
      type: 2
      value: You'll need to dock with the mothership to update your ship design.
        I'll refrain from judging it... loudly.
      baseValue: 
      context: 
      aiTranslated: 0
      keptEnglish: 0
    - key: worldController.assemblerPanelIncreaseLevelDialog.0
      type: 2
      value: Spend credits here to raise an item's level. Stats improve, so yer old
        gear doesn't fall behind.
      baseValue: 
      context: 
      aiTranslated: 0
      keptEnglish: 0
    - key: worldController.assemblerPanelIncreaseRarityDialog.0
      type: 2
      value: Boost an item's rarity by sacrificing a stronger one of the same kind.
        Higher rarity means more room for modifiers, without losing what ya've already
        got.
      baseValue: 
      context: 
      aiTranslated: 0
      keptEnglish: 0
    - key: worldController.assemblerPanelReplaceModifierDialog.0
      type: 2
      value: This lets ya lift a modifier off one item and stick it on another. Costs
        credits, and unless it's a schematic, the donor's scrap after.
      baseValue: 
      context: 
      aiTranslated: 0
      keptEnglish: 0
    - key: worldController.firstStarSkirmishDialog.0
      type: 2
      value: Some of the enemy ships are disrupting the gateways. Eliminate those
        ships to proceed!
      baseValue: 
      context: 
      aiTranslated: 0
      keptEnglish: 0
    - key: worldController.firstStarWarzoneDialog.0
      type: 2
      value: Multiple enemies closing on your position. Don't worry, I'll send reinforcements
        to assist!
      baseValue: 
      context: 
      aiTranslated: 0
      keptEnglish: 0
    - key: worldController.firstStarRescueDialog.0
      type: 2
      value: Our ally's hyperdrive is damaged. Defend them until they can get it
        back online!
      baseValue: 
      context: 
      aiTranslated: 0
      keptEnglish: 0
    - key: worldController.firstStarInterceptDialog.0
      type: 2
      value: We've intercepted a group of transport ships carrying valuable cargo.
        Destroy them before they escape with it!
      baseValue: 
      context: 
      aiTranslated: 0
      keptEnglish: 0
    - key: worldController.firstStarTraderDialog.0
      type: 2
      value: Trading vessels like this don't take sides. Not that we're in any position
        to argue.
      baseValue: 
      context: 
      aiTranslated: 0
      keptEnglish: 0
    - key: worldController.firstStarEliteDialog.0
      type: 2
      value: Eliminate the enemies quickly, an elite foe is incoming.
      baseValue: 
      context: 
      aiTranslated: 0
      keptEnglish: 0
    - key: worldController.increaseRarityDialog.0
      type: 2
      value: Well now, yer movin' up in the galaxy! Bring me yer gear, and I'll upgrade
        it's rarity. Let's make it shine!
      baseValue: 
      context: 
      aiTranslated: 0
      keptEnglish: 0
    - key: worldController.replaceModifierDialog.0
      type: 2
      value: Right, here's something new. I can transfer modifiers between equipment
        now. Let's get creative, eh?
      baseValue: 
      context: 
      aiTranslated: 0
      keptEnglish: 0
    - key: worldController.firstNebulaDialog.0
      type: 2
      value: Visibility is suboptimal. Activating exhaust vents.
      baseValue: 
      context: 
      aiTranslated: 0
      keptEnglish: 0
    - key: worldController.firstNebulaDialog.2
      type: 2
      value: Much better. You can toggle them back closed if you wish to hide.
      baseValue: 
      context: 
      aiTranslated: 0
      keptEnglish: 0
    - key: worldController.firstNebulaDialog.3
      type: 2
      value: Like a coward?
      baseValue: 
      context: 
      aiTranslated: 0
      keptEnglish: 0
    - key: worldController.firstNebulaDialog.4
      type: 2
      value: Nooo, like a predator, stalking their prey! I can't fire weapons or
        boost without opening them though.
      baseValue: 
      context: 
      aiTranslated: 0
      keptEnglish: 0
    - key: worldController.firstDebrisMoltenAsteroidsDialog.0
      type: 2
      value: Molten asteroids detected. Collision will apply Burning, dealing thermal
        damage over time and rapidly increasing ship heat. Thermal damage is amplified
        in this region.
      baseValue: 
      context: 
      aiTranslated: 0
      keptEnglish: 0
    - key: worldController.firstDebrisFrozenAsteroidsDialog.0
      type: 2
      value: Frozen debris field ahead. Impact may inflict Frozen, reducing speed
        and weapon output by fifty percent while draining heat quickly. Cold damage
        is enhanced in this area.
      baseValue: 
      context: 
      aiTranslated: 0
      keptEnglish: 0
    - key: worldController.firstDebrisRadioactiveAsteroidsDialog.0
      type: 2
      value: Radioactive asteroids present. Collision applies stacking Radioactive
        damage that bypasses shields. Avoid repeated impacts. Radiation damage is
        amplified in this area.
      baseValue: 
      context: 
      aiTranslated: 0
      keptEnglish: 0
    - key: worldController.firstDebrisCorrosiveAsteroidsDialog.0
      type: 2
      value: Corrosive debris detected. Impact causes Corroding, allowing enemies
        to critical strike you. Corrosive damage is increased in this area.
      baseValue: 
      context: 
      aiTranslated: 0
      keptEnglish: 0
    - key: worldController.firstDebrisInvaderNebulaDialog.0
      type: 2
      value: Void particles detected. Contact will trigger Burning, applying thermal
        damage over time and increasing heat. Do not fly through them unnecessarily.
      baseValue: 
      context: 
      aiTranslated: 0
      keptEnglish: 0
